# CQ-A6 — When the "impossible or disproportionate effort" exemption applies, what obligation
# remains in force?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT A NEW CQ. CQ-A6 is one of the 27 FROZEN competency questions
# (methodology/competency_questions.json, theme A, articles ["14"], eval_level false), with no
# .rq until now only because no Article-14 graph existed. Additional operationalisation of a
# frozen question — the CQ-B1…B4 / CQ-C5x precedent (2026-07-10). No CQ is added or edited.
#
# Frozen probe: "14(5)(b) protective-measures duty arises inside the exception and is not
# defeated by it."
#
# HOW THE LINK IS MADE (T3-C, Zied 2026-08-04 — read before judging):
# 14(5)(b) is TWO things in one Point: an exemption GROUND (first half) and an affirmative
# controller DUTY that arises in that case (second half). There is NO exception->obligation
# property in the TBox, and minting one would be a TBox change the Art-14 unit is not authorized
# to make. So the shared node is the GROUNDING POINT: both the Exception and the Obligation are
# groundedIn ex:art14-p5-b, and the join across that shared Point is what makes the remaining
# duty reachable FROM the exemption ground. This is the SAME idiom as CQ-C5x (SURFACE-C,
# 2026-07-10), which joins an Art-13 condition to an Art-6 basis through their shared Point.
#
# The scope guard `ex:art14-p5 hasPoint ?sharedProvision` is REQUIRED, not decorative: without
# it the pattern also matches Art-12, where exc-12-2/exc-12-3 share their grounding Paragraph
# with obligations that they DO defeat — which is the opposite relationship and would be a wrong
# answer, not a bonus row.
#
# Regime: (needs materialisation) for the inferred super-types; correct on a plain graph too.
#
# Expected over the 5-file union: 1 row —
#   ex:exc-art14-5-b-impossible-disproportionate @ ex:art14-p5-b -> ex:obl-art14-5-b-protective-measures
#
# ⚠ If this returns 0 rows, that is a FINDING to report, NOT a reason to rewire the graph
# (Art-14 brief v3.1 §6.2).
#
# ⚠ LEGALLY UNCORROBORATED (brief §2.5): asserting a duty that arises BECAUSE an exemption
# applies is a legal characterisation. The modelling decision is taken; the doctrinal
# confirmation is carried to the finished-work legal review alongside I8.
PREFIX gdprkg: <https://w3id.org/gdprkg#>
PREFIX ex:     <https://w3id.org/gdprkg/data#>
SELECT ?exemptionGround ?sharedProvision ?remainingObligation
WHERE {
  ?exemptionGround a gdprkg:Exception ;
                   gdprkg:groundedIn ?sharedProvision .
  ?remainingObligation a gdprkg:Obligation ;
                       gdprkg:groundedIn ?sharedProvision .
  ex:art14-p5 gdprkg:hasPoint ?sharedProvision .
}
ORDER BY ?sharedProvision ?remainingObligation
